Air traffic controllers in Balboa undergo training at the BAA's training facility in Sant Cristòfor, which includes radar simulation and tower simulation equipment. Controller certification requires approximately three years of training, including classroom instruction, simulation, and on-the-job training under supervision.

== Financials ==

The Air Navigation Services Division operates at a net deficit, with annual operating costs of approximately $69 million against air navigation charge revenue of approximately $40 million. The deficit of approximately $30 million is covered by the BAA's cross-subsidy from airport revenue, principally the surplus generated by [[Sant Cristòfor International Airport]].

